# KILN Master File — Complete Session State
Version 5.0 — 2026-10-04
Supersedes 4.0 of 2026-10-03

## What changed in 5.0

Three assumptions in 4.0 were tested and disproven. They are recorded
here so no one re-tries them.

1. AVX2 fused matmul is not a speedup on Tier 0. Measured 0.13x
   (7.8x SLOWER) versus the scalar C matmul. The scalar C matmul
   auto-vectorizes with GCC -O3 -mavx2 and is memory-bound, not
   compute-bound. Hand-written AVX2 with cvtepu8_epi32 widening is
   slower than what the compiler already emits.

2. The dense autoregressive path is not the product. It is the
   correctness reference. It runs Qwen2.5-1.5B correctly at
   0.15 tok/s. Ollama runs the same model on the same hardware
   roughly 10x faster. That gap is real and must be closed, but the
   dense path will never reach the mission target. The mission target
   requires MoE, ternary, and streaming.

3. The registry, scheduler, and DAG plan exist as types but are not
   wired into the forward pass. Every matmul in `transformer.rs`
   calls a hardcoded function. This is the central architectural gap
   and Phase 1.5 exists to close it.

## Purpose of this file

Restores the entire project state if a session is interrupted. Paste
