## Section 13A — Rule KILN-E37 — The Roadmap Is the Only Source of Truth

The roadmap file `KILN MASTER ROADMAP AND RULES SET.md` is the sole
authoritative description of what KILN is, what it does, what it does
not do, and in what order. It is not a summary. It is not a reference.
It is the specification.

Consequences:

1. If the code disagrees with the roadmap, the code is wrong.
2. If a session's plan disagrees with the roadmap, the plan is wrong.
3. If the AI assistant proposes a direction that is not in the
   roadmap, the assistant must first update the roadmap and get it
   confirmed before writing any code. No exceptions.
4. If a section of the roadmap is proven wrong by measurement, the
   roadmap is edited to record the correction before the code is
   changed. The correction is a first-class deliverable.
5. The session entry point is a quote from the roadmap, not a
   paraphrase.
6. Drift between the roadmap and the repository is the highest-
   severity defect in the project. It is fixed before any other work.

The roadmap lives at `~/KILN-MASTER-ROADMAP-AND-RULES-SET.md` (the
canonical location, outside the repo) and at
`~/Desktop/KILN/KILN MASTER ROADMAP AND RULES SET.md` (working copy,
untracked by git). Both must be identical at end of session.

